Chapter 'colossalreactors' 'Colossal Reactors' 'colossal_reactors:reactor_controller' 'tech' 'Start with a small affordable reactor, then expand your power infrastructure.' -showlines
Q 'start' 'Big Power, Small Beginnings' 'check' '' 'xp:50' -size 1.5 -icon 'colossal_reactors:reactor_controller' -desc 'Begin with a small reactor. GSPack uses steel, graphite, iron, copper and a Basic Control Circuit for the early components; no antimatter, Nether Star or endgame core is required. Read the controller feedback and JEI before starting it.'
Q 'steel' 'A Steel Framework' 'tag:c:ingots/steel@alltheores:steel_ingot' 'start' 'xp:50' -desc 'Obtain steel using your preferred processing route. The early reactor recipes use the shared steel tag.'
Q 'graphite' 'Graphite' 'colossal_reactors:graphite_ingot' 'start' 'xp:50' -desc 'Produce Graphite using its installed JEI recipe.'
Q 'fuel' 'Uranium Supply' 'colossal_reactors:uranium_ingot' 'start' 'xp:75' -desc 'Collect reactor fuel and confirm the controller accepts it before automating input. Keep fuel and waste storage separate.'
Q 'casing' 'Affordable Reactor Casings' 'colossal_reactors:reactor_casing*24' 'steel,graphite' 'xp:100' -desc 'GSPack crafts eight casings per batch from steel, graphite and iron. Start small instead of building a huge empty shell.'
Q 'controller' 'Reactor Controller' 'colossal_reactors:reactor_controller' 'casing' 'xp:100' -size 1.5 -desc 'The controller uses an early Mekanism Basic Control Circuit. Its feedback explains whether your reactor structure is valid.'
Q 'rods' 'Fuel Rods' 'colossal_reactors:reactor_rod*4' 'graphite,casing' 'xp:75' -desc 'Fuel rods use iron bars and graphite. Place them according to the controller and mod structure rules.'
Q 'control_rods' 'Rod Controller' 'colossal_reactors:rod_controller' 'rods' 'xp:75' -desc 'Control rods let you regulate output. Begin conservatively and watch the live controller readouts.'
Q 'resource_port' 'Fuel and Waste Access' 'colossal_reactors:resource_port' 'casing' 'xp:75' -desc 'Resource ports provide the reactor input/output interface. Configure their modes and separate the fuel and waste paths.'
Q 'power_port' 'Connect Your Machines' 'colossal_reactors:power_port' 'casing' 'xp:75' -desc 'An affordable copper/redstone power port exports energy. Use an FE-compatible cable and storage.'
Q 'glass' 'A Window Into the Reactor' 'colossal_reactors:reactor_glass' 'casing' 'xp:50' -opt -desc 'Reactor Glass is an optional visual upgrade. Keep the required controller, ports and structure blocks in place.'
Q 'builder' 'Reactor Builder' 'colossal_reactors:reactor_builder' 'controller' 'xp:75' -opt -desc 'Use the Builder tool if its installed behavior suits your structure. It is optional for this beginner route.'
Q 'structure' 'A Valid Small Reactor' 'check' 'controller,rods,control_rods,resource_port,power_port' 'xp:150;table:uncommon' -size 1.5 -shape 'hexagon' -desc 'Assemble a small shell, required rod arrangement, controller and ports. Follow controller feedback until it reports a valid structure. Tick this only after the structure forms.'
Q 'cooling' 'Understand the Readouts' 'check' 'structure' 'xp:75' -desc 'Read fuel, heat and output information. Check the installed moderator/cooling options in JEI and the mod interface; do not assume that a larger reactor is automatically more efficient.'
Q 'first_power' 'Your First Reactor Power' 'check' 'fuel,cooling' 'xp:200;table:rare' -size 1.5 -desc 'Supply a small fuel amount, enable the reactor and verify that energy reaches a connected machine or storage block. Tick after observing actual generation.'
Q 'automation' 'Reliable Fuel Handling' 'check' 'first_power' 'xp:100' -desc 'Automate supported fuel input and waste output. Test a full input/output cycle and ensure storage can accept the results.'
Q 'turbine_casing' 'The Next Power Project' 'colossal_reactors:turbine_casing' 'first_power' 'xp:100' -opt -desc 'Turbines are an optional expansion after your first working reactor. Review their fluid and structure requirements before building.'
Q 'turbine_controller' 'Turbine Controller' 'colossal_reactors:turbine_controller' 'turbine_casing' 'xp:100' -opt -desc 'The turbine has its own controller and valid-structure rules.'
Q 'blades' 'Turbine Internals' 'colossal_reactors:turbine_blade;colossal_reactors:turbine_rod' 'turbine_controller' 'xp:75' -opt -desc 'Plan rotor and blade geometry using the mod feedback. This is not required to start the reactor route.'
Q 'complete' 'A Dependable Power Plant' 'check' 'automation' 'xp:300;table:epic' -size 1.5 -shape 'gear' -desc 'Maintain a valid, fueled reactor with working energy export and resource handling. Expand only when your machines need it. This is an optional power route, not a new gate on the first Moon trip.'
